#
# The primary goal of gitlab-nginx is to provide a **more secure, auditable,
# and production-hardened** way to install and configure GitLab CE with
# Certbot and nginx in external nginx mode.
#
# Key improvements in 2.0.0:
#   • Full integration of GitLab CE (Omnibus) with strict external nginx mode
#   • Separation of GitLab web (HTTPS) and SSH hostname to solve Cloudflare
#     port 22 proxy limitations
#   • Strict 13-step installation sequence (Certbot → Nginx → GitLab → Config)
#   • Persistent storage for main domain, additional domains, email, and
#     gitlab SSH hostname under /etc/letsencrypt/
#   • Continued use of dedicated least-privilege user "nginx-adm"
#   • Dated backup policy extended to gitlab.rb
#   • Clear client-side ~/.ssh/config instructions (Step 13)
